        "original_id": "4557f61a-1aaa-51d1-aaed-48eb78c630f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ai-Ling Lee, Jean-Marc Vallée\n- Places: Singapore, Los Angeles, California\n- Roles: sound editor, re-recording mixer, audio engineer, film director\n- Films: Bruce Almighty, Spider-Man 2, Mr. & Mrs. Smith, Tangled, Wild, The Maze Runner, Deadpool, La La Land\n- Events: 89th Academy Awards\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Sound Editing, Academy Award for Best Sound Mixing\n\nFacts:\n- Ai-Ling Lee is a Singaporean sound editor, re-recording mixer, and audio engineer who works in Los Angeles, California.\n- Ai-Ling Lee worked on the films Bruce Almighty (2003), Spider-Man 2 (2004), and Mr. & Mrs. Smith (2005).\n- Ai-Ling Lee worked on the film Tangled (2010).\n- Wild is a 2014 American biographical survival drama film directed by Jean-Marc Vallée.\n- Ai-Ling Lee worked on the films Wild (2014), The Maze Runner (2014–15), and Deadpool (2016).\n- Ai-Ling Lee worked on the critically acclaimed musical-drama La La Land.\n- At the 89th Academy Awards, Ai-Ling Lee received two nominations for La La Land: Academy Award for Best Sound Editing and Academy Award for Best Sound Mixing.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
